    {
      "name": "app",
      "files": ["App.tsx", "index.tsx"],
      "layer": "ui",
      "$comment": "A module may be declared by file instead of by folder, and these five entries are why. `App.tsx`, `index.tsx`, `types.ts`, `constants.ts` and `utils.ts` live at the root of the repository, so no prefix caught them and the gate never opened them — for its whole life. That is not a detail: `types.ts` is imported by 25 of the 34 modules and imports six, so it closes the graph on its own. Measuring the modular monolith without it produced a green gate over 27 mutually reachable modules. See ADR-105."
    },
    {
      "name": "types.ts",
      "files": ["types.ts"],
      "layer": "foundation",
      "$comment": "Declared one by one rather than as a single `shared kernel` because each is fixed on its own and the budget has to be able to fall one at a time: `constants.ts` only imports types and is inert, `types.ts` is the knot (F3-07), and `utils.ts` is a file with a utility's name holding prompt composition (F3-08). `foundation` and not `domain` because the layer is decided by what sits below: `lib` imports them, so they are below `lib`. Calling them domain would have turned the finding into `lib imports domain`, naming the consumer instead of the cause."
    },
    { "name": "constants.ts", "files": ["constants.ts"], "layer": "foundation" },
